I think I may have done a bad job explaining things.

When using the non-`Func<>` path, sizing is taken frmo the passed in drawable [immediately](https://github.com/ppy/osu-framework/blob/master/osu.Framework/Graphics/Containers/DelayedLoadWrapper.cs#L76-L80) via the `Content_Set`.

In the case this doesn't happen, the wrapper is zero-size. If the wrapper's location is off the edge of the screen, it won't begin counting up to load the drawable in.

![2024-01-17 23 22 37@2x](https://github.com/ppy/osu/assets/191335/180955f0-d8d2-43aa-85c6-ab9c57da0163)


In other words, it never gets to the point of constructing / setting `Content`.

It could be tested by moving the song bar slightly off-screen.

```diff
diff --git a/osu.Game.Tournament.Tests/Components/TestSceneSongBar.cs b/osu.Game.Tournament.Tests/Components/TestSceneSongBar.cs
index 95d6b6d107..0f7b4406c5 100644
--- a/osu.Game.Tournament.Tests/Components/TestSceneSongBar.cs
+++ b/osu.Game.Tournament.Tests/Components/TestSceneSongBar.cs
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 using osu.Game.Beatmaps.Legacy;
 using osu.Game.Tournament.Components;
 using osu.Game.Tournament.Models;
+using osuTK;
 
 namespace osu.Game.Tournament.Tests.Components
 {
@@ -35,8 +36,9 @@ public override void SetUpSteps()
             AddStep("create bar", () => Child = songBar = new SongBar
             {
                 RelativeSizeAxes = Axes.X,
-                Anchor = Anchor.Centre,
-                Origin = Anchor.Centre
+                Anchor = Anchor.BottomLeft,
+                Origin = Anchor.BottomLeft,
+                Position = new Vector2(5),
             });
             AddUntilStep("wait for loaded", () => songBar.IsLoaded);
         }

```

> If the wrapper's location is off the edge of the screen, it won't begin counting up to load the drawable in

Okay this makes more sense thanks.

That said something like this does the job just as fine:

```diff
diff --git a/osu.Game.Tournament/Components/TournamentBeatmapPanel.cs b/osu.Game.Tournament/Components/TournamentBeatmapPanel.cs
index 4e0adb30ac..221ea7075a 100644
--- a/osu.Game.Tournament/Components/TournamentBeatmapPanel.cs
+++ b/osu.Game.Tournament/Components/TournamentBeatmapPanel.cs
@@ -194,7 +194,10 @@ private partial class NoUnloadBeatmapSetCover : UpdateableOnlineBeatmapSetCover
 
             // Use DelayedLoadWrapper to avoid content unloading when switching away to another screen.
             protected override DelayedLoadWrapper CreateDelayedLoadWrapper(Func<Drawable> createContentFunc, double timeBeforeLoad)
-                => new DelayedLoadWrapper(createContentFunc, timeBeforeLoad);
+                => new DelayedLoadWrapper(createContentFunc, timeBeforeLoad)
+                {
+                    RelativeSizeAxes = Axes.Both
+                };
         }
     }
 }

```

Forcing the eager construction of the drawables is probably fine too but I'd say the practice of using 0x0 DLWs is the core footgun here.
